A||||3||SibERThuG||gauge lights||||8||
Z||000000||SibERThuG||06-18-2000||10:53 PM||||I replaced my stock AM/FM/Cassete with a CD player. Now my gauge lights are out. The fuse is good. Could it be my dimmer switch?? My dimmer switch is the brown wire right??!! What does that get hooked up to, because it's not hooked up to anything now. If this is it, please tell me. If I am incorrect, can you solve this??||||reg||8
Z||000001||Oreif||06-18-2000||11:10 PM||||The Gray Wire (on the radio connector) is the panel lamp lights. If this is hooked up incorrectly to something other than a light it could cause a problem. If it shorted it won't blow a fuse because of all the lights in the path but the lights won't light up. If the radio has a dimmer input then hook the gray wire to it if it does not make sure the wire isn't shorting. The brown is the light output from the headlight/dimmer switch. Make sure the brown and the gray are not tie together inside the radio. Only hook up brown or gray.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 06-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||SibERThuG||06-18-2000||11:15 PM||||If it shorted how do I fix it??||||reg||5
Z||000003||Oreif||06-18-2000||11:23 PM||||If it is shorted, pull radio and inspect wire for any nicks or cuts. Then tape them up with electrical tape (including the end) and then tape it out of the way||||reg||1
